                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="ielts-listening-question-item"> • <span>UK</span><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">29</strong><select data-qnum="29" name="question_29" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 29 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. This country suffered the most severe loss of life.">A. This country suffered the most severe loss of life.</option><option value="B. The impact on agriculture was predictable.">B. The impact on agriculture was predictable.</option><option value="C. There was a significant increase in deaths of young people.">C. There was a significant increase in deaths of young people.</option><option value="D. Animals suffered from a sickness.">D. Animals suffered from a sickness.</option><option value="E. This country saw the highest rise in food prices in the world.">E. This country saw the highest rise in food prices in the world.</option><option value="F. It caused a particularly harsh winter.">F. It caused a particularly harsh winter.</option></select></span></div>
